    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντᾴδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sing in answer,</i> esp. of the partridge, <i>answer</i>
			when another calls, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὡς μαχούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					614a11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mir.</u>
				845b25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				4.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Μούσαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pisc.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς φθεγγομένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.794c
				</span></i>
			; <i>cry out at one,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγὼ δ᾽, ἢν τοῦτο δρᾷς, ἀντᾴσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					887
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφῇ ἀντᾳσθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.112
				</span></i>
			.</div>
